{"id":133942529684686,"type":"artist","name":"Robyn Hitchcock","artist":null,"year":1953,"weight":14,"info":{"tags":["singer-songwriter","alternative","folk","indie","folk-rock"],"country":"GB","begin":"1953-03-03","kind":"Person","similar":["Robyn Hitchcock and The Egyptians","Camper Van Beethoven","Joe Henry","Julian Cope","John Wesley Harding","The Minus 5","Richard Thompson","Bob Mould","Billy Bragg","Robyn Hitchcock & the Venus 3"],"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Robyn_Hitchcock%2C_Oct._2012.jpg?width=500","bio":"Robyn Hitchcock es un poeta, pintor, actor, cantante y compositor británico nacido en 1953. Su primera grabación la hizo en el año 1976 con la banda The Soft Boys. Se separaron en 1981, y Hitchcock comenzó su carrera en solitario con el nombre Robyn Hitchcock & The Egyptians. Las influencias de Hitchcock incluyen a Bob Dylan y la psicodelia de Syd Barrett. Sus letras son serias, expresadas de una forma poco seria. Su disco de 2002, \"Robyn Sings\", era un tributo a Bob Dylan incluyendo sólo canciones suyas."},"works":[{"id":129253396908336,"type":"album","name":"Black Snake Diamond","artist":"Robyn Hitchcock","year":1981,"weight":6,"yt":"ekxYfWOpm_o","src":"books","from":{"books":[{"name":"Scaruffi","title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000 (Piero Scaruffi)"}],"podcasts":[],"lists":[],"n_lists":0}},{"id":112437746782904,"type":"album","name":"Black Snake Diamond Role","artist":"Robyn Hitchcock","year":1981,"weight":12,"yt":"_4MR1YO6v3I","src":"charts,musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":52032266791182,"name":"Scaruffi 1980s","rank":686,"scaruffi":7.0},{"id":114383129677180,"name":"RYM Top — Psychedelia — Psychedelic Pop","rank":89,"scaruffi":7.0}],"n_lists":2}},{"id":43180486878949,"type":"album","name":"I Often Dream of Trains","artist":"Robyn Hitchcock","year":1984,"weight":11,"yt":"MzXb4a2v_dU","src":"books,musthear","from":{"books":[{"name":"Scaruffi","title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000 (Piero